{
  "_comment": "Spawn pools for the roulette. Tier-first: category -> tier -> group -> { sections, count, min, max, icon }. A single-group reward (rolls=1) picks ONE random group from the tier and spawns exactly `count` creatures. A multi-group reward (rolls>1, e.g. 'x3') picks that many groups (independently - the same group can come up more than once) and spawns a RANDOM count for each, in [min, max] - default (no min/max set) is [max(1,count-1), count], so it just works without touching this file; set min/max on a specific group to hand-tune it (min=max=1 pins a boss-type group to always roll exactly 1 even in a x3 draw). Each creature is a random pick from that group's `sections`. `label` overrides the group key shown on the overlay / in the in-game message. `icon` is a public/ path for the overlay reel (mutant-icons/, patch-icons/); omitted where no icon exists yet. Mutant sections verified against this GAMMA install's actual creature configs (temp/mutant-sections-full.txt); weak/normal/strong variants split Basic/Advanced/Expert, count 1/2/3. A few types have no natural weak/normal/strong split (zombies, chimeras, poltergeists) - flagged below. tushkano and poltergeist sections are best-guess, not fully verified - check in game. Edit freely - unknown sections are skipped by the Lua side.",

